From 3d57cf547751c1890c4c18732964a04b61080675 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duck-brain <duck-brain@localhost>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 19:25:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] duck-brain P4-P6: live skill command, phase clocks, the
 policy's HOME and action scale

P4 - a skill with live = true is fed the client's twist (after the
deadman, before cmd_alpha) instead of its constant command: the roller
stride and Fish are steered while they run.

P5 - a network may read a clock after its 61 inputs (63): which one is
in its observation_names metadata - swizzle_phase (ride v2, crouch v2:
phi += 2 pi f dt, f = min(|cmd0| / 0.615, 1.5) Hz, 0 at |cmd0| <= 0.05,
x (1 - u/0.3) for the crouch depth u = cmd1) or fish_phase (phi =
2 pi t / phase_period_s from the start of the skill). The 61 blocks are
checked against observation_names at load; a fish network needs its
period, nothing else may have one.

P6 - observation and targets are relative to the network's own HOME
(default_joint_pos) and scaled by its action_scale when its metadata
says them; bring-up, holds and the limp-fall pose go to the walking
policy's HOME. A skill's params.action_scale still wins.
